@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Method / document navigation. Scope-independent process/navigation; provider or runner examples are not MVP prerequisites.
title Resumefolio | Elicitation working cycle
skinparam backgroundColor #101827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F1F5F9
skinparam hyperlinkColor #A9D0FF
skinparam dpi 216
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #9FB2CD
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #1C3453
 BorderColor #9FB2CD
 FontColor #F1F5F9
 DiamondBackgroundColor #49351C
 DiamondBorderColor #F2BA72
 StartColor #F1F5F9
 EndColor #F1F5F9
}
start
:Select an actor goal and accepted scope references;
:Review existing decisions and identify genuine gaps;
:Choose technique, material / participants and rationale;
repeat
 :Capture actual source statements and observations;
 :Explore success, alternatives, failure, access and lifecycle;
 :Separate interpretations, assumptions and solution ideas;
 :Summarize and obtain actual clarification / feedback;
 :Record unresolved questions and evidence limits; <<#49351C>>
repeat while (Further clarification available and needed now?) is (yes) not (no)
if (Material questions still unresolved?) then (yes)
 :Assign owner, next action and dependent review gate; <<#49351C>>
 :Mark unreviewed interpretations explicitly;
else (no known gap)
 :Record actual review outcome and its scope; <<#173B34>>
endif
:Hand reviewed needs and open questions to analysis;
:Maintain source, scenario and requirement links;
stop
legend bottom
Record only sessions, participants and feedback that actually occurred.
Reviewed needs are inputs to analysis; they are not an accepted requirements baseline.
Revisit elicitation when later evidence exposes new uncertainty.
endlegend
@enduml
